cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalisation, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Existence and uniqueness for the Blasius boundary-layer problem, formalised in Lean 4"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 / Mathlib formalisation of section 2 of H. Weyl, "On the differential
  equations of the simplest boundary-layer problems", Annals of Mathematics 43 (1942):
  existence and uniqueness of the solution of w''' + 2 w w'' = 0 on [0, infinity) with
  w(0) = w'(0) = 0 and w'(z) -> k, and of the Blasius problem f''' + f f'' = 0,
  f(0) = f'(0) = 0, f'(eta) -> 1. The Lean code was generated with the AI assistant
  Claude (Anthropic) and is verified by the Lean kernel.
authors:
  - family-names: Schaffarczyk
    given-names: Alois Peter
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9357-3232"
    affiliation: "University of Applied Sciences Kiel"
version: 1.0.1
date-released: 2026-11-18
license: Apache-2.0
